        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: bind RunPod release to exact claims",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- bind RunPod destructive operations to exact local claims containing provider ID and pod name\n- require explicit `--reclaim` adoption for unclaimed or legacy pods; never silently retarget an existing claim\n- re-read the pod under the release lock and verify both ID and name before deletion\n- reject ambiguous exact, normalized-name, and derived-lease lookups instead of adopting the first provider result\n- preserve exact created-pod identity through readiness failure cleanup\n- add a cleanup-armed, isolated-state RunPod live lifecycle canary and top-level live-smoke dispatch\n\nCloses https://github.com/openclaw/crabbox/issues/801\n\n## Verification\n\nCurrent candidate: `003fee96a021ea3a6d9a741e552e81c00a35d0fe`\n\nLocal validation across the candidate stack:\n\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD`\n- `go test -race ./...` on parent `77eaf1f7aec792af3b63fd7516550e76b2eea9ec`\n- `go vet ./...`\n- `scripts/check-docs.sh`\n- `node --test scripts/*.test.js` (379 passed)\n- focused RunPod race tests covering mismatch rollback, explicit reclaim, retarget refusal, ambiguous-name/lease refusal, and exact-claim deletion\n- `node --test scripts/live-runpod-smoke.test.js` (7 passed)\n- `node --test scripts/live-smoke.test.js` on the exact current head (51 passed, including RunPod dispatch)\n- full-branch autoreview clean with no accepted/actionable findings\n\nHosted validation on the exact current candidate: all 11 checks passed.\n\n## Pre-merge live gate\n\nAuthenticated RunPod access is not available in the maintainer environment. Keep this PR unmerged until `scripts/live-runpod-smoke.sh` passes on this exact head, proving real pod create, SSH command execution, exact-claim stop, and zero-residue inventory cleanup; alternatively record an explicit item-specific waiver.\n\n## Security / configuration\n\nNo new persisted-secret requirement. The live canary accepts `CRABBOX_RUNPOD_API_KEY` or `RUNPOD_API_KEY` only from the process environment and isolates its Crabbox state.\n",
